{"path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment1.md","content":"🚨 **BLOCKING: action-time mutex re-check inverts the `mutexExcludeSelf` contract — leaked holder stacks can no longer drain (fa#1068/#577 regression)**

`validationMutexHeldByAnother` runs for **every** `validate_pr` rule with `query.mutex` — including `revalidate-armed` and `revalidate-armed-green`, whose candidates **self-hold** `ai_validating` (their query requires the label) and whose queries set `mutexExcludeSelf: true`.

The query-time scan (`js/sm/sources/githubSource.js:473-501`) implements exclude-self as:

```js
var selfHolds = holdsMutex(candidate);
var blocked = !selfHolds && items.some(function (it) { ...another holder... });
```

A self-holding candidate is **never** blocked — that is the fa#1068/#577 fix: a leaked multi-holder stack drains oldest-first **through the revalidate rules** when the verdict rules cannot match (live: both heads green-with-missing-CI + BLOCKED → ~40 min full-queue freeze until a manual strip).

The new action-time check blocks on ANY other holder regardless of self-hold:

```js
if (num === ticket.prNumber) continue; // self never blocks self
return num;
```

**Freeze trace** (approved PRs A + B both holding `ai_validating`, the dispatched validation CI never ran — the #1068 profile): `merge-validated` / `fail-validation` / `sweep-stale-validating` / `unarm-stale-validation` match nothing; `validate-armed` defers at query time (global mutex form); `revalidate-armed` A reaches the arm → probe finds holder B → **refused**; candidate B symmetric → refused. Nothing ever dispatches the missing CI, so the verdict rules can never match: the queue freezes until a human strips a label. The double-arm state this PR exists to fix (#1194+#1215) is itself a 2-holder stack — whenever the extra holder is not red/green-CLEAN, the drain is exactly this path.

The in-code comment claims *"Same semantics as githubSource's scan (blocked holders invisible, exclude-self honored, self never blocks self)"* — for the exclude-self rules it is not: githubSource's exclude-self means a **self-holding candidate ignores other holders**; here it still gets blocked by them.

**Fix (mirror githubSource exactly)** — track `selfHolds` while scanning and return 0 for a self-holding candidate under `mutexExcludeSelf`:

```js
var selfHolds = false, otherHolder = 0;
for (var i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    // ...existing label/blocked/among filtering...
    if (num === ticket.prNumber) { selfHolds = true; continue; }
    otherHolder = num; break;
}
if (q.mutexExcludeSelf && selfHolds) return 0; // #577 parity: a self-holder drains the stack
return otherHolder;
```

Or the simpler equivalent: `if (q.mutexExcludeSelf) return 0;` up front — the revalidate rules re-dispatch CI on an **already-armed** candidate and never create a second holder, so the re-check has nothing to protect on those rules; its two intended arm sites (latch-skip arm, post-dispatch arm) both live on validate-armed, which has no `mutexExcludeSelf`.

Please add a test: `revalidate-armed` candidate (self-holding, checks `none`) + a second live approved holder → the re-dispatch **proceeds** (today it is refused), and the mirror case (candidate NOT holding the mutex) stays refused.
"}

